THE SHORT VERSION

This is the source of my business website. It is public so the work can be
read and judged — by a client deciding whether to hire me, or by anybody
curious how it is built. It is not open source, and the branding is not
yours to use under any circumstances.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

- Read the source code.
- Quote short extracts in a review, article or teaching material, with
  attribution.
- Borrow a technique. Ideas are not owned; this file is about the code and
  the brand, not about how anyone solves a problem.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

- Use this code, in whole or in part, in another site or project.
- Copy the design, layout, stylesheets or page structure into another site.
- Redistribute, republish, sell, sublicense or host this software.
- Remove or alter this notice.


BRAND ASSETS — NEVER

The SMOALD name, the wordmark, the bolt device, the logo files in assets/,
and the red-and-gold identity are trade marks of this business. No permission
is given to use them, in any form, altered or unaltered, for any purpose. That
includes "inspired by" versions.

This is not the same as the code restriction above, and there is no version of
asking that makes it available.


THE WRITING

The page copy — service descriptions, the about page, pricing explanations and
the legal pages — took real work and is covered by the same restriction as the
code. Rewriting a competitor's site by swapping the nouns is obvious to anyone
who reads both.


